# Installed as /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/000-keys-only.conf by `setup.sh _ssh_keys_only`.
# sshd keeps the first value it reads: the temporary override from `setup.sh _ssh_allow_password`
# must come first. It lives in /var/run, which macOS wipes at boot.
Include /var/run/sshd-allow-password-temporarily.conf
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
AuthenticationMethods publickey
PermitRootLogin no
